        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Metagenics makes clean protein powders with sensible labels, and Perfect Protein Whey is a genuinely good whey isolate: 20 g of protein in 100 calories with a short ingredient list. The brand's own testing and its place in SuppCo's TESTED program are real, but no Metagenics protein carries NSF Certified for Sport, and the brand does not publish heavy-metal numbers.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The deciding factor is price. At $3.12 to $3.33 per 25 g for Perfect Protein and far more for BioPure and the UltraMeal shakes, you pay two to six times the going rate for protein you can get elsewhere. Buy Metagenics when a practitioner you trust specifies it; otherwise, a certified or clean retail protein is the better buy.
          </p>
